  "worked_solution": "The direction vectors of the lines are ${v}_{1}=\u27e81,2,-3\u27e9$ and ${v}_{2}=\u27e8-1,0,3\u27e9$, respectively. These vectors are parallel to the plane but not to each other.\n\nWe also know that the point $C(1,\\sqrt{2},-1)$ lies on the plane and its position vector is $c=\u27e81,\\sqrt{2},-1\u27e9.$  \n\nSo, the corresponding parametric equation of the plane is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =c+s{v}_{1}+t{v}_{2} \\\\ r & =\u27e81,\\sqrt{2},-1\u27e9+s\u27e81,2,-3\u27e9+t\u27e8-1,0,3\u27e9,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\\end{aligned}\n$$",
